        <div>
          <span
            class=" num "
            >02
          </span>
          <h3>Bite Mapping</h3>
          <p
            class=" pdesc "
          >
            Ensuring the veneers work with your natural bite, not against it. The protocol verifies clearance for
            chewing and speech without forcing pressure on adjacent teeth.
          </p>
          <p
            class=" pfail "
          >
            <strong>How generic snap-ons get this wrong </strong>
            Generic snap-ons can shift when you talk or eat because they weren't designed against your specific bite,
            leading to lisping, clicking sounds, and discomfort.
          </p>
          <p
            class=" pmeans "
          >
            <strong>What this means for you </strong>
            Your veneers stay put when you eat, talk, or laugh. No clicking sounds. No shifting.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
