        <div>
          <span
            class=" num "
            >03
          </span>
          <h3>Tooth Proportions</h3>
          <p
            class=" pdesc "
          >
            Width-to-height ratios refined per tooth, not factory-default. Each tooth on the veneer is individually
            proportioned: central incisors slightly wider than laterals, canines with a subtle point, premolars with
            appropriate width.
          </p>
          <p
            class=" pfail "
          >
            <strong>Why factory veneers fail here </strong>
            Cheap snap-ons make every tooth the same width and shape. The result reads as obviously artificial on close
            inspection, especially in photos.
          </p>
          <p
            class=" pmeans "
          >
            <strong>What this means for you </strong>
            Your veneers look like a refined version of natural teeth, not a row of identical white tiles.
          </p>
        </div>
