          <span
            class=" num "
            >05
          </span>
          <h3>Edge Aesthetics</h3>
          <p
            class=" pdesc "
          >
            Translucency and finish at the biting edge, so teeth read like enamel, not plastic. Natural teeth have a
            subtle translucency at the edge. The protocol replicates this property in the resin.
          </p>
          <p
            class=" pfail "
          >
            <strong>Where mass-market veneers break down </strong>
            Most snap-on veneers use uniform-opacity plastic that reads as obviously fake in any photo where the biting
            edge is visible.
          </p>
          <p
            class=" pmeans "
          >
            <strong>What this means for you </strong>
            Your teeth look like enamel in photos, video calls, and direct sunlight. Not like a costume.
          </p>
        </div>
